    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d751">

                <pb facs="0691" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/3044</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Spring Rice</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d751-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1457</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to the memorandum dated
                    November 15, 1917,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d751-f2"/> of the British Embassy and
                    the Department’s reply thereto dated January 3, 1918,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d751-f3"/> concerning the provisioning of all Serbian prisoners of
                    war in enemy countries by the American National Red Cross, I have the honor
                    further to inform you that a credit will be extended to the Serbian Government,
                    and that the Red Cross is now ready to make purchases for shipments of food for
                    this purpose.</p>
                <p>Before making a final decision in this matter, however, I would be pleased to
                    have a definite expression of the views of the British Government that it
                    concurs in the proposed provisioning of all Serbian prisoners of war by the
                    American National Red Cross, and that the shipments of food to be sent to
                    Switzerland for distribution to the prisoners will be facilitated as much as
                    possible by His Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
